# CODEOWNERS — mechanical separation of duties (NIST AC-5, CM-5, AIC-2)
#
# CODEOWNERS is what turns "the author doesn't approve" from a convention into a control.
# Combined with branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners" + "Dismiss stale
# approvals" + no administrator bypass), a PR cannot merge without an approval from an
# identity other than the author.
#
# Replace the placeholder teams with your real GitHub teams or usernames.
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default — every change needs an engineering review by a non-author
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                               @your-org/engineering

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The process itself. Changing the rules requires the people accountable for them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md                      @your-org/security @your-org/engineering-leads
/docs/                          @your-org/engineering-leads
/docs/compliance/               @your-org/compliance @your-org/security
/docs/11-ai-agent-controls.md   @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/security
/docs/12-ai-feature-governance.md @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/security
/process/gates/                 @your-org/security @your-org/engineering-leads

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PIPELINE GATES ITSELF. A PR that edits workflows can disable every other
# control in this repo, so it requires security review without exception. (CM-5)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/security @your-org/platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @your-org/security @your-org/engineering-leads
/.github/dependabot.yml         @your-org/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent and command definitions are configuration items under change control.
# An edit here can relax a control as effectively as editing a workflow — this is
# the quietest way to weaken the system. (AIC-8)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.claude/agents/                @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/security
/.claude/commands/              @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/engineering-leads
/.claude/settings.json          @your-org/security @your-org/platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security-relevant code paths. Adjust to your actual layout — these patterns are
# the point, not the specific directory names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/auth/**                      @your-org/security
**/authn/**                     @your-org/security
**/authz/**                     @your-org/security
**/session/**                   @your-org/security
**/crypto/**                    @your-org/security
**/secrets/**                   @your-org/security
**/middleware/**                @your-org/security
**/migrations/**                @your-org/security @your-org/data

# Infrastructure and configuration (CM-6, CM-7)
/infra/                         @your-org/security @your-org/platform
/terraform/                     @your-org/security @your-org/platform
**/Dockerfile                   @your-org/security @your-org/platform
**/*.tf                         @your-org/security @your-org/platform

# Dependency manifests — supply chain (SR-3, SR-4, SR-11, AIC-7)
**/package.json                 @your-org/security
**/package-lock.json            @your-org/security
**/requirements*.txt            @your-org/security
**/pyproject.toml               @your-org/security
**/go.mod                       @your-org/security
**/Cargo.toml                   @your-org/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI feature code. Prompts are code — a prompt change is a behavior change that
# ships to production, and it gets the same review as any other. (AIC-8)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/prompts/**                   @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/security
**/evals/**                     @your-org/ai-risk
**/guardrails/**                @your-org/ai-risk @your-org/security
**/*.prompt.*                   @your-org/ai-risk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence is an audit artifact. It is generated, never hand-edited — a hand-edited
# scan report is a fabrication regardless of intent. (AU-9)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/evidence/                      @your-org/compliance @your-org/security
